 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "kiddushin.60b.21",
   "daf": "60b",
   "sentenceId": 20,
   "he": "״עַל מְנָת שֶׁאַרְאֵךְ בֵּית כּוֹר עָפָר״. תָּאנָא: לֹא נִתְכַּוְּונָה זוֹ אֶלָּא לִרְאוֹת מִשֶּׁלּוֹ. וְאִם הֶרְאָהּ בַּבִּקְעָה – אֵינָהּ מְקוּדֶּשֶׁת. פְּשִׁיטָא! לָא צְרִיכָא דְּנָקֵיט בְּדִיסְתּוּרָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna further teaches: If a one says to a woman: You are hereby betrothed to me «on the condition that I will show you a beit kor of earth,» she is betrothed, provided that he possesses such land. A Sage «taught» (Tosefta 3:6): The woman «intended to see only his own» land. The mishna further teaches: «And if he showed» her a plot of land «in a valley, she is not betrothed.» The Gemara asks: This is «obvious;» after all, this land does not belong to him. The Gemara answers: «No,» it is «necessary» in a case «where he maintains» the field «as a sharecropper [distora],» i.e., he owns a share in it. Nevertheless, as the land does not belong to him she did not have this field in mind, and consequently she is not betrothed."
  }
 ],
